From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SUM <sum@sexidium.local>
Date: Sat, 20 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Sexidium Linear region timing instrumentation (L1-TIMING)

Loop-1 Stage 2 (SUM): lock-free timing instrumentation for the Linear
read/write/flush paths. No behaviour change on the ANVIL path
(byte-identical); no hot-interface signature changes; no synchronized added
on hot record paths (LongAdder/LongAccumulator only); no Bukkit lookups; no
new threads; micros via System.nanoTime/1000.

P0: all RegionFileStorage hunks byte-exact vs 0009/0011-post context
(S1/S3 carry trailing return/brace context so no duplication; S4 indents
match predecessor 16sp/20sp/12sp/8sp/4sp; every context line byte-compared
against the predecessor patch text with python). P1: no batch-level flush
increments (flushDirty untouched; flushOne records failures +
filesFlushed-on-ok only; doFlush clean-no-op records nothing via didIo
guard). P2: reportCacheMiss wired at both miss fall-throughs; dead
reportRead/Write/Flush/Load/Failure bridges deleted (file-level record*
already forwards; storage stays zero-field). P3: close() needs no special
case (didIo guard covers it). P5: fixed "ternary" comment (no ternary at
the hit site). NMS hooks: LinearRegionStats (per-file view), snapshots()
map on coordinator, sexidium$stats() on LinearRegionFile + RegionFileStorage
(zero new storage fields, sexidium$ prefix, no signature changes, no Bukkit
imports, no new threads/synchronized on hot paths).

New file net/sexidium/LinearRegionTimings.java carries the public records
(LinearTimings(count,totalMicros,maxMicros,avgMicros) with
of(LongAdder,LongAdder,LongAccumulator) + EMPTY, LinearRegionStats per-file
view, and LinearFolderSnapshot with read/write/flush/load groups +
markDirty/filesFlushed/failures/oversizeRejects/evicts/cacheHits/cacheMisses
+ dirtyDepth). Coordinator and region-file hunks below only ADD
fields/methods and finally-recording; the storage hunks only delegate to
the coordinator (zero new storage fields).

